---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CAPE — Corridor Accumulation and Portfolio Exposure | Narrows"
  description="CAPE calculates your fleet's aggregate exposure to corridor disruption events. Powered by the Narrows CDM and TIDE accumulation model."
>

<style>
/* ── Demo notice ── */
.demo-notice {
  background: var(--gold-pale);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(240,180,41,0.3);
  padding: 12px var(--s4);
  text-align: center;
}
.demo-notice-inner {
  max-width: var(--max-w);
  margin: 0 auto;
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  font-weight: 300;
}
.demo-notice-inner strong {
  color: var(--navy);
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* ── Hero ── */
.cape-hero {
  padding: 120px var(--s4) var(--s5);
  max-width: var(--max-w);
  margin: 0 auto;
}
.cape-kicker {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--text-tertiary); margin-bottom: var(--s2);
}
.cape-kicker::before { content: ''; width: 32px; height: 1px; background: var(--gold); }
.cape-hero h1 {
  font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 54px); font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy);
  line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: var(--s2);
}
.cape-hero h1 em { font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; color: var(--blue-light); }
.cape-hero-lead {
  font-size: 17px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7;
  font-weight: 300; max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: var(--s4);
}
.cape-hero-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--s2); align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.btn-primary-lg {
  display: inline-block; background: var(--navy); color: #fff;
  font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; padding: 13px 28px; border-radius: 5px;
  text-decoration: none; transition: background 0.15s; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}
.btn-primary-lg:hover { background: var(--blue); }
.btn-ghost-lg {
  display: inline-block; border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text-secondary);
  font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 5px;
  text-decoration: none; transition: border-color 0.15s, color 0.15s;
}
.btn-ghost-lg:hover { border-color: var(--navy); color: var(--navy); }

/* ── What it is ── */
.cape-what {
  background: var(--surface);
  border-top: var(--rule-light); border-bottom: var(--rule-light);
  padding: var(--s5) var(--s4);
}
.cape-what-inner {
  max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto;
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--s6);
  align-items: center;
}
@media (max-width: 768px) { .cape-what-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s4); } }
.cape-what-text h2 {
  font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy);
  letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: var(--s2);
}
.cape-what-text p {
  font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7;
  margin-bottom: var(--s2);
}
.cape-what-text p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.cape-distinction {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;
}
.cape-distinction-row {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 14px; align-items: start;
  background: #fff; border: var(--rule-light); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px;
}
.cape-distinction-label {
  font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--gold); background: var(--navy); padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 3px;
  white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1.5;
}
.cape-distinction-text strong { display: block; font-size: 13px; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 2px; }
.cape-distinction-text span { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-tertiary); line-height: 1.5; }

/* ── TIDE strip ── */
.tide-strip {
  background: var(--navy);
  padding: var(--s5) var(--s4);
}
.tide-strip-inner { max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; }
.tide-strip-head {
  display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: var(--s4);
}
.tide-strip-label {
  font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--gold);
}
.tide-strip-sub { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); }
.tide-numbers {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 12px;
  margin-bottom: var(--s3);
}
@media (max-width: 900px) { .tide-numbers { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 480px) { .tide-numbers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.tide-num {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.07); border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 18px 20px;
}
.tide-num-label { font-size: 10px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.tide-num-value { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.tide-num.accent .tide-num-value { color: var(--gold); }
.tide-num-note { font-size: 11px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.35); line-height: 1.4; }
.tide-cascade-note {
  background: rgba(240,180,41,0.12); border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 12.5px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65); line-height: 1.6;
}
.tide-cascade-note strong { color: var(--gold); }

/* ── How it works ── */
.cape-how {
  padding: var(--s5) var(--s4);
  max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto;
}
.cape-how h2 {
  font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy);
  letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: var(--s4);
}
.cape-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: var(--s3); }
@media (max-width: 768px) { .cape-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.cape-step {
  border: var(--rule-light); border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;
}
.cape-step-num {
  font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  color: var(--gold); text-transform: uppercase;
}
.cape-step h3 { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }
.cape-step p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
.cape-step.locked { background: var(--surface); }
.cape-step.locked .cape-step-num { color: var(--text-tertiary); }
.cape-step-gate {
  display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--navy); background: rgba(240,180,41,0.15);
  border: 1px solid rgba(240,180,41,0.3); border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 4px 10px; margin-top: auto;
}

/* ── Privacy + CTA ── */
.cape-cta-section {
  background: var(--surface);
  border-top: var(--rule-light);
  padding: var(--s5) var(--s4);
  text-align: center;
}
.cape-cta-section h2 {
  font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy);
  letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: var(--s2);
}
.cape-cta-section p {
  font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7;
  max-width: 520px; margin: 0 auto var(--s3);
}
.cape-privacy {
  font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-tertiary);
  margin-top: var(--s3); display: flex; align-items: center;
  justify-content: center; gap: 6px;
}
</style>

<!-- Demo notice -->
<div class="demo-notice">
  <p class="demo-notice-inner">
    <strong>Demonstration.</strong> This version runs against a sample portfolio with fixed positions.
    The full version of CAPE connects to a live cargo portfolio and updates in real time.
    <a href="mailto:fysh@narrows.io?subject=CAPE full access" style="color:var(--blue);font-weight:500;margin-left:6px">Request access.</a>
  </p>
</div>

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="cape-hero">
  <div class="cape-kicker">Narrows analytics</div>
  <h1>Corridor Accumulation<br>and <em>Portfolio Exposure</em></h1>
  <p class="cape-hero-lead">
    CAPE tells you what is physically at risk on a single bad day. Load your vessel portfolio,
    select a corridor event, and get aggregate exposure by vessel class, corridor, and scenario severity.
    Powered by the Narrows CDM and TIDE accumulation model.
  </p>
  <div class="cape-hero-actions">
    <a href="/cape.html" class="btn-primary-lg" target="_blank">Open CAPE demo</a>
    <a href="mailto:fysh@narrows.io?subject=CAPE access request" class="btn-ghost-lg">Request full access</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What it is -->
<section class="cape-what">
  <div class="cape-what-inner">
    <div class="cape-what-text">
      <h2>Two questions. Two different answers.</h2>
      <p>
        The Narrows simulator answers the structural question: what share of Japan's crude imports
        depends on Hormuz each year? That is a dependency figure. It tells you what is exposed.
      </p>
      <p>
        CAPE answers the underwriting question: if Hormuz restricts today, how much cargo value
        is simultaneously in transit through the corridor right now, at the worst point in the
        seasonal calendar, including the approach window where vessels cannot economically divert?
        That is an accumulation figure. It tells you what is at risk.
      </p>
      <p>
        These are different numbers for different audiences. Both are in CAPE.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cape-distinction">
      <div class="cape-distinction-row">
        <div class="cape-distinction-label">CDM</div>
        <div class="cape-distinction-text">
          <strong>Annual structural dependency</strong>
          <span>What percentage of a country's imports transit a given corridor each year. The strategic exposure view.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cape-distinction-row">
        <div class="cape-distinction-label">CAPE</div>
        <div class="cape-distinction-text">
          <strong>Portfolio corridor exposure</strong>
          <span>Your vessel book's aggregate VaR under a named corridor scenario. The underwriting view.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cape-distinction-row">
        <div class="cape-distinction-label">TIDE</div>
        <div class="cape-distinction-text">
          <strong>Market accumulation at risk</strong>
          <span>Total cargo in transit through a chokepoint at seasonal peak, including cascade effects on diversion routes. The reinsurance and ILS view.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TIDE strip -->
<section class="tide-strip">
  <div class="tide-strip-inner">
    <div class="tide-strip-head">
      <span class="tide-strip-label">TIDE</span>
      <span class="tide-strip-sub">Strait of Hormuz — accumulation at risk</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tide-numbers">
      <div class="tide-num">
        <div class="tide-num-label">Baseline (avg day)</div>
        <div class="tide-num-value">$25.7B</div>
        <div class="tide-num-note">Annual flow divided by 365, weighted by transit duration</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tide-num">
        <div class="tide-num-label">Seasonal peak</div>
        <div class="tide-num-value">$30.5B</div>
        <div class="tide-num-note">January — winter LNG demand drives peak flows</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tide-num accent">
        <div class="tide-num-label">Event horizon</div>
        <div class="tide-num-value">$36.5B</div>
        <div class="tide-num-note">Seasonal peak plus 3-day approach window — the insurer's at-risk number</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tide-num">
        <div class="tide-num-label">War risk PML</div>
        <div class="tide-num-value">$3.97B</div>
        <div class="tide-num-note">Event horizon at 15% severity, weighted attachment rate</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tide-cascade-note">
      <strong>Cascade effect:</strong> When Suez closes, Cape of Good Hope accumulation spikes
      <strong>71%</strong> above normal — more cargo is simultaneously at sea on the diversion route.
      A Lloyd's syndicate writing Cape war risk has correlated exposure to Red Sea events.
      TIDE models cascade ratios for all corridors.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- How it works -->
<section class="cape-how">
  <h2>How CAPE works</h2>
  <div class="cape-steps">
    <div class="cape-step">
      <div class="cape-step-num">Step 01 — Free demo</div>
      <h3>Illustrative fleet</h3>
      <p>
        Twelve representative vessels across all major corridors are pre-loaded: VLCCs on Hormuz,
        LNG carriers on Qatar routes, Neopanamax containers through Panama, Capesize bulk through
        Malacca. Each vessel carries full JWC listing status, CII rating, diversion cost, and
        cargo value. Run any scenario immediately.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cape-step locked">
      <div class="cape-step-num">Step 02 — Full access</div>
      <h3>Your portfolio</h3>
      <p>
        Upload your own vessel book as a CSV or enter vessels individually. CAPE maps each vessel
        to its corridor exposure and computes aggregate VaR, diversion cost, and JWC status
        across your actual positions.
      </p>
      <span class="cape-step-gate">Request access</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cape-step locked">
      <div class="cape-step-num">Step 03 — Full access</div>
      <h3>TIDE accumulation output</h3>
      <p>
        Full TIDE report: event horizon by corridor, seasonal peak calendar, cascade ratios
        for diversion routes, vessel-count breakdown, and war risk PML by scenario severity.
        Exportable as a plain-text report for use in capital models.
      </p>
      <span class="cape-step-gate">Request access</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="cape-cta-section">
  <h2>Run your own book</h2>
  <p>
    CAPE is available to marine underwriters, reinsurers, P&I clubs, and commodity desks.
    Full access includes portfolio upload, all TIDE accumulation outputs, and corridor
    scenario export.
  </p>
  <div class="cape-hero-actions" style="justify-content:center">
    <a href="/cape.html" class="btn-primary-lg" target="_blank">Open CAPE demo</a>
    <a href="mailto:fysh@narrows.io?subject=CAPE access request" class="btn-ghost-lg">Request access</a>
  </div>
  <p class="cape-privacy">
    <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
      <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2"/>
      <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/>
    </svg>
    Portfolio data is processed in your browser and never transmitted to any server.
  </p>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
